The attached image illustrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles enhance the expression of costimulatory molecules (CD40, CD80, and CD86) on dendritic cells, indicating their activation. Flow cytometry histograms show a significant increase in the mean fluorescence intensity for CD80 and CD86 in dendritic cells treated with Nano-11 (black line) compared to an untreated control (gray line), with a modest increase for CD40. This activation is a crucial step in promoting an effective adaptive immune response, supporting Nano-11's role as a potent vaccine adjuvant by providing "signal 2" for T cell activation.